1h7|n|Confirmation of anything established; ratification; as, the affirmation of a law. ; The act of affirming or asserting as true; assertion; -- opposed to negation or denial. ; That which is asserted; an assertion; a positive statement; an averment; as, an affirmation, by the vender, of title to property sold, or of its quality. ; A solemn declaration made under the penalties of perjury, by persons who conscientiously decline taking an oath, which declaration is in law equivalent to an oath.	v:1t6s,100,3~1t6s,100,3
